<title>USA: Robotic Vision buys Systemation for stock.</title>
<headline>Robotic Vision buys Systemation for stock.</headline>
<dateline>HAUPPAUGE, N.Y. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robotic Vision Systems Inc said on Tuesday that it has acquired Systemation Engineered Products Inc, based in New Berlin, Wisconsin, for Robotic stock valued at about $24 million.</p>
<p>Systemation, a tape-and-reel and tube and tray based component processing systems company, ahd revenues of about $29 million and net income of about $1.48 million for its fiscal year ended March 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
